MODEL FIDELITY CHECK (real tape)
======================================================================
  bin-mean LSQ fit:  cost ~= 1.2795e-04 n + -1.0417e-09 n^2   R^2=0.9196
  cost increasing in size: True   (rank corr 0.88)
  cost per USD: 0.54 bps (smallest bin) -> 0.71 bps (largest bin)
  NOTE: the quadratic-in-n term is an AMM (xy=k) property derived analytically;
        the CEX tape confirms positive, size-increasing execution cost and sets
        the linear fee/spread scale.  Curvature on a CEX book is venue-specific.

